From eac6a57f29e08d176001adcc294bb6a4b02456f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:21:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: host PCM over the real-time proxy ports
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The host side of the AFE real-time proxy ports, gate 2 of the call audio
bridge for Bluetooth headsets:

- q6afe: a client API for the proxy ports: register a port with a
  callback (AFE_SERVICE_CMD_REGISTER_RT_PORT_DRIVER), map and unmap a
  buffer (AFE_SERVICE_CMD_SHARED_MEM_MAP_REGIONS), and read from RX or
  write to TX without waiting (RT_PROXY_PORT_READ_V2/WRITE_V2); the
  callback gets every data acknowledgement and port status event.
- q6afe-rt-proxy: a small sound card of its own ("RTProxy") with a
  playback PCM that writes the uplink to RT_PROXY_TX_1 and a capture PCM
  that reads the downlink from RT_PROXY_RX_1. A period timer sends one
  command per period, the acknowledgement advances the pointer, as the
  downstream msm-pcm-afe driver does. The buffer goes to the DSP with
  the SMMU stream id of the node's iommus, as q6asm-dai does.
- the Pro1-X board: the rt-proxy node under the AFE service.

Built, not yet run on the device.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model wrote the change from the downstream audio-kernel sources)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=none; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=claude-opus-5-5; retrieval=none
